{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וזה אשר תעשה", :translit "v'zeh asher ta'aseh", :gloss "and this is what you shall make"} {:he "וזה אשר תעשה על המזבח", :translit "v'zeh asher ta'aseh al ha-mizbei'ach", :gloss "and this is what you shall make on the altar"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וזה אשר תעשה" "וזה אשר תעשה על המזבח"]}], :frame {:text "The altar is understood as a vehicle of atonement: regarding the altar of the burnt offering, Scripture says 'and this is what you shall make on the altar' (Exodus 27:8), and the Talmud states that the altar effects atonement (Zevachim 88b). Noah, upon exiting the ark, builds an altar and offers sacrifices (Genesis 8:20), which the midrash reads as an act of atonement (Bereshit Rabbah 34:9). The Ba'al HaTurim links the rare phrase shared by the ark-construction command and the altar-construction command to suggest the ark itself served an atoning function.", :sources ["Exodus 27:8" "Genesis 8:20" "Zevachim 88b" "Bereshit Rabbah 34:9"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וזה אשר תעשה" "וזה אשר תעשה על המזבח"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וזה אשר תעשה", :refs ["Genesis 6:15" "Exodus 29:38"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וזה אשר תעשה על המזבח", :refs ["Exodus 29:38"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:04:38.836293707Z", :model "glm-5.2"}